    "created_at": "2017-05-25T21:09:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-25T21:09:16Z",
    "body": "OMG, I just looked at the tests we have in Chrome, and some of them assume that the origin-clean flag is reset, but the tests pass by accident because they are poorly written.  These tests were inherited from WebKit, so they probably have the same issue.\r\n\r\nIMHO, we could and should reset the origin-clean flag, since that behavior is more permissive and still keeps cross-origin data safe.\r\n\r\nI am kind of torn about what to do here.\r\nIs the current behavior 100% interoperable? Have you looked at IE/Edge? (I don't have windows here)\r\nIf all major browsers are doing the same thing, maybe we should just change the spec to reflect interoperable behavior. Otherwise, I think we should fix the implementations (and the tests).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
